{
  "id": "ferryporter-law",
  "term": "Ferry–Porter law",
  "definition": "Ferry–Porter law is the visual finding that temporal acuity, such as the ability to detect faster flicker, increases roughly logarithmically as light level rises. In plain terms, brighter illumination makes the visual system respond faster over a wide range of intensities.",
